                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Actually… basic fun. This is a Words/Puzzle game with a comedy angle. The graphics are adequate; the music is okay. The story is made up of several short bits, poking fun at familiar characters and actors.\n\nNo bugs or crashes.\n\nOverall, entertaining but not that funny. Most of the time it’s just nonsense wording that still scores points. On the bright side, it’s very light to play if you just want something short between meals. It includes cards and achievements, though the last two demand extreme grinding. Very cheap, especially in bundles. Online is dead. You can certainly have fun with it, just don’t expect more than giggles—especially if you’re not familiar with the characters and their backgrounds. That’s likely the case for younger generations, so it ends up kinda niche.",
